  "headline": "Capital of Empires, Capital of India",
  "short_description": "India's capital blends Mughal monuments, colonial-era New Delhi and a modern metropolis into one sprawling city.",
  "about": "Delhi has served as the seat of power for successive empires — from the Delhi Sultanate to the Mughals to the British Raj — and today is India's political capital and a gateway for most international visitors.\n\nLocated in northern India on the banks of the Yamuna river, bordered by Haryana and Uttar Pradesh.\n\nA meeting point of Mughlai, Punjabi and modern Indian cultures, with a thriving arts, food and nightlife scene.\n\nHome to major mosques, temples, gurdwaras and the Bahá'í Lotus Temple, reflecting India's religious diversity.",
  "history": "Delhi's recorded history spans over a millennium, with seven historic cities layered within the modern metropolis, from the Tomars and the Delhi Sultanate through Mughal Shahjahanabad to Lutyens' New Delhi.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Indira Gandhi International Airport (airport)\n- New Delhi Railway Station (railway)\n- Kashmere Gate ISBT (bus terminal)\n- Anand Vihar ISBT (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Hindi, English, Punjabi, Urdu\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March",
  "ideal_duration_text": "3–4 days",
  "nearest_airport": "Indira Gandhi International Airport (DEL)",
  "nearest_railway_station": "New Delhi Railway Station (NDLS)",
